## 2. BACKGROUND AND STATE OF THE ART — 2026 UPDATE

### 2.1 Natural Photosynthesis: The Engineering Baseline

The net reaction of oxygenic photosynthesis is:

$$6\,\text{CO}_2 + 6\,\text{H}_2\text{O} \xrightarrow{h\nu} \text{C}_6\text{H}_{12}\text{O}_6 + 6\,\text{O}_2$$

Real-world solar-to-biomass efficiencies for terrestrial plants are typically 0.1–1 %, far below the theoretical maximum of ~4.6 %. The SST targets a solar-to-product conversion efficiency ≥ 15 % using the updated 33.6 % flexible tandem canopy — a 15-fold to 150-fold improvement over biology that constitutes the fundamental engineering justification for the SST concept.

### 2.2 Perovskite-Silicon Tandem Photovoltaics: The 2025–2026 Revolution

Four interconnected breakthroughs have transformed the SST photovoltaic specification since v3.0:

**Flexible tandem record (Nature, 2026):** Wang et al. demonstrated a certified **33.6 %** power conversion efficiency in a flexible perovskite/crystalline-silicon (c-Si) tandem solar cell, with a record open-circuit voltage of Voc = 2.015 V — rivalling its rigid counterpart. This is the number that directly governs the SST canopy specification, since flexible modules are required for the phyllotactic leaflet geometry.

**Rigid tandem record (Matter, May 2026):** Researchers at NIMTE (Chinese Academy of Sciences), Soochow University, Taizhou University, and S.C. Exact Equipment Co. achieved a certified **32.89 %** rigid tandem via a peak-selective passivation strategy that suppresses electrical leakage at the pyramid-textured silicon surface. This represents the current module-pathway benchmark.

**Absolute cell record:** LONGi Green Energy's certified **34.85 %** tandem cell (NREL, April 2025) — which employs bilayer LiF/EDAI₂ interface passivation at the perovskite/C₆₀ junction — crosses the Shockley-Queisser single-junction silicon limit of 33.7 % for the first time. This confirms the theoretical headroom available to the SST as module-scale processes mature.

**Industrial-scale stability (Hanwha Q CELLS, 2026):** Certified 30.8 % on industrial Q.ANTUM silicon bottom cells with 95 % efficiency retention after 1,000 hours of maximum power point tracking at 25 °C — the key industrial durability benchmark.

**Commercial availability:** Oxford PV's Fraunhofer CalLab-certified 26.9 % module efficiency on a 60-cell residential format (2024) defines the current commercial floor, with tandem modules entering broad commercial supply projected for 2027.

The SST v4.0 therefore upgrades its canopy target from 28.0 % (v3.0) to **33.6 % flexible module efficiency**, increasing the electrical power budget by a further 20 % relative to v3.0 and 53 % relative to v2.0.

**Lead toxicity:** The primary SST design continues to prioritise lead-free tin-based perovskites for urban public spaces. 2D/3D perovskite phase engineering and multi-layer hermetic encapsulation evaluated in WP1 serve as an engineering pathway for lead-containing variants where tin alternatives fall short of the efficiency target.

### 2.3 Electrochemical MOF DAC: Two New 2026 Paradigms

The most significant materials-science advance for the SST trunk reactor is the emergence of *electrically conductive* MOFs capable of solid-state electrochemical CO₂ capture, reported in two landmark 2025–2026 papers:

**Ni₃(HITP)₂ with Ni-BDI units (JACS 2025):** This electrically conductive MOF integrates nickel bis(diimine) units as the CO₂-active sites. Electrochemical cycling (potential control of the Ni centre's redox state) drives reversible carbamate formation and release via a one-electron reaction per Ni site. Reported performance: **96 % capacity utilisation, 98 % Faradaic efficiency, stable over 50 capture-release cycles, resistant to O₂, H₂O, NO₂, and SO₂ interference.** This resistance to co-adsorption of water and criteria pollutants is the critical real-world advantage over thermally regenerated amine sorbents.

**Cu₃(HHTP)₂ (RSC J. Mater. Chem. A, 2026):** DFT calculations confirm that efficient CO₂ capture is mediated by the combination of the redox-active copper atom and the aromatic HHTP ligand, with reversible CO₂ electrosorption demonstrated by DEMS. This provides a copper-based alternative to the nickel system, with distinct voltage-window and kinetic characteristics valuable for the multi-material screening in WP1.

**Farha group molecular-level architecture (JACS 2025):** A comprehensive framework for designing MOF pore geometry and functional group placement to maximise trace-CO₂ (400 ppm) capture — directly applicable to ambient-air conditions. Computational screening using Latent Variable Gaussian Process and Multi-Objective Batch-Bayesian Optimisation (LVGP-MOBBO) identified all Pareto-optimal MOFs by searching only ~1 % of the design space, providing the precise screening pipeline adopted in SST WP1.

**Electrochemical regeneration energy:** With these conductive MOF architectures, the regeneration energy is electrochemical (Faradaic) rather than thermal. The estimated energy per mole CO₂ released is:

$$E_{regen} = \frac{n \cdot F \cdot \Delta V_{redox}}{\eta_{Faradaic}}$$

For a one-electron process (n = 1), ΔV_redox ≈ 0.3–0.5 V, and η_Faradaic = 0.96–0.98:

$$E_{regen} \approx \frac{1 \times 96485 \times 0.4}{0.97} \approx 39.8\ \text{kJ mol}^{-1}$$

This is a **6-fold reduction** relative to thermal swing regeneration (230–800 kJ mol⁻¹ thermal equivalent) and a factor of 2× below even the Sargent-Farha 2026 electrochemical surface mineralisation estimate of 40–80 kJ mol⁻¹, placing the SST v4.0 MOF contactor at the lowest-energy end of any reported DAC regeneration cycle.

### 2.4 Direct Air Electrowinning: 2026 Operational and Laboratory Frontiers

Four 2026 developments define the DAE architecture adopted in SST v4.0:

**Phlair Electra (Rotterdam, operational):** One of Europe's first operational DAE plants, capturing 260 t CO₂ yr⁻¹ via the Hydrolyzer technology. Operates on behind-the-meter solar, using up to 3× less energy than thermal DAC. Captured CO₂ is permanently mineralised via the Phlair-Paebbl partnership.

**Delft/ACS Sustainable Chem. Eng. (2026):** A dual-sorbent integrated system in which an amine-functionalised solid sorbent captures CO₂ from air, is regenerated by rinsing with an aqueous carbonate-rich solution, and the resulting bicarbonate-rich solution is fed directly to a zero-gap electrolyser for conversion to syngas. The study identifies the pH-swing between rich and lean solutions as the dominant design parameter, governed almost exclusively by electrolyser sizing — a key insight for SST reactor engineering in WP2.

**Solid-electrolyte reactor for direct DAC-to-ethylene (Energy & Fuels, 2024–2026):** A solid electrolyte electrochemical cell capturing CO₂ and H₂O simultaneously from air and converting them to ethylene at a full-cell voltage of only **0.6 V**, with ~80 % energy efficiency and continuous operation. This dramatically lower voltage compared to liquid alkaline systems (2.0–2.5 V) is incorporated as the primary DAE architecture in SST v4.0.

**Continuous methanol from air-captured CO₂ (Carbon Capture Sci. Technol., 2026):** Sakamoto et al. demonstrate continuous electrolytic methanol synthesis from air-captured CO₂ at ordinary temperature and pressure — validating the concept of integrating product flexibility (ethylene vs. methanol vs. formate) into a common DAE platform, which the SST v4.0 adopts as a mode-switching capability.

### 2.5 Carbon Mineralisation: 2026 Accelerated Pathways

**CarbFix (Iceland):** CO₂-charged water injected into basalt mineralises to solid carbonate within 2 years; over 60 % of injected CO₂ mineralises within 4 months. The Silverstone project aims to capture >95 % of CO₂ from the Hellisheiði plant from 2025. This provides the geological permanence baseline calibrating the SST olivine model.

**Enhanced weathering — Project Vesta:** Finely ground olivine spread on beaches to accelerate weathering kinetics and enhance ocean alkalinity. The SST root cassette generalises this to urban subsurface, with particle size optimised by the shrinking-core model in WP5.

**CemCycle / PCC harvest:** Precipitated calcium carbonate from the Zone A CKD buffer is sold as construction aggregate, directly improving carbon economics.

### 2.6 Passive Daytime Radiative Cooling: Design Basis

PDRC surfaces achieve sub-ambient temperatures by simultaneously reflecting solar radiation and emitting longwave infrared through the 8–13 µm atmospheric transparency window to the ~2.7 K effective sky. The SST trunk and canopy undersides are coated with SiO₂/TiO₂/PDMS multilayer stacks providing solar reflectance ρ_solar > 0.95 and longwave emissivity ε_LW > 0.95. At a net cooling power of:

$$P_{cool} = \varepsilon_{LW} \sigma T_s^4 - Q_{solar,absorbed} - Q_{conduction}$$

values of 40–100 W m⁻² sub-ambient cooling power have been reported experimentally, corresponding to surface temperatures 3–8 °C below ambient. The SST ENVI-met simulations (WP6) are calibrated to these experimentally validated ranges, not to idealised calculations.

### 2.7 AI Control Architecture: 2026 State of the Art

**PINNs for electrochemical systems (2026):** A PINN-based charge allocation framework embedding charge conservation and State-of-Charge constraints directly as loss terms achieves real-time adaptive control of PV battery systems under varying irradiance and load (Batteries, January 2026). A parallel PINN framework for solid oxide electrochemical cells achieves a maximum relative error of 1.2 % compared to high-fidelity pseudo-two-dimensional models, while being 20.8 % faster than traditional numerical methods. These results directly validate the PINN approach for the SST edge control layer.

**Hybrid Neural ODE + PINN (iScience, 2025):** Combines neural ordinary differential equations with PINNs and LSTM/Transformer sequential models for physically consistent, continuous-time state estimation — the architecture adopted for the SST Layer 1/Layer 2 interface.

**Open-weight LLMs (2026):** Meta's Llama 4 (released April 2025) and Mistral's current generation provide 7B–70B parameter open-weight models suitable for local inference. In April 2026, Meta Superintelligence Labs released Muse Spark as Llama's successor. The vLLM inference framework (PagedAttention, now a PyTorch Foundation hosted project) enables efficient INT4-quantised inference at ≈8 W on ARM edge servers — the computational basis for the SST Layer 3 orchestrator.

**EU CRCF regulatory integration:** The CRCF Regulation EU/2024/3012 is now in force. Its first delegated act — establishing DACCS, BECCS, and biochar certification methodologies — was adopted in February 2026, with certification bodies accepting applications from April 2026. The four QU.A.L.ITY criteria (quantification, additionality, long-term storage, sustainability) define the verification architecture that the SST LLM compliance engine must operationalise. A public consultation on the post-2030 implementation package closed in May 2026.

