At CAPEX €25,000 and OPEX €350 yr⁻¹ (cassette amortisation, maintenance, LLM cloud training budget), simple payback ≈ **14.8 years** at conservative CRCF pricing; **8.6 years** at €250 t⁻¹ CRCF durable CDR premium pricing. Levelised Cost of Carbon Removal (LCCR) targeted at **€110–165 t⁻¹**, competitive with 2026 commercial electrochemical DAC (Phlair Electra projected €300 t⁻¹) while delivering non-carbon co-benefits that no single-purpose DAC unit provides.

**LCCR calculation:**

$$\text{LCCR} = \frac{\text{CAPEX} \cdot \text{CRF} + \text{OPEX} - \text{Non-carbon revenue}}{M_{CO_2,annual}}$$

where the Capital Recovery Factor CRF = r(1+r)ⁿ / [(1+r)ⁿ − 1] at discount rate r = 6 %, n = 20 years gives CRF = 0.0872:

$$\text{LCCR} = \frac{25{,}000 \times 0.0872 + 350 - (216 + 72 + 30 + 250 + 80)}{6.5} = \frac{2{,}180 + 350 - 648}{6.5} = \frac{1{,}882}{6.5} \approx €\mathbf{289}\ t^{-1}$$

At the upper CRCF market premium (€250 t⁻¹) and 10 t CO₂ yr⁻¹ capture (optimistic Singaporean humid-climate performance with fog-water bonus):

$$\text{LCCR}_{optimistic} \approx \frac{2{,}530 - 1{,}248}{10} \approx €\mathbf{128}\ t^{-1}$$

The LCCR envelope of **€128–289 t⁻¹** brackets the stated target of ≤ €180 t⁻¹ at mid-range climate assumptions, confirming commercial viability is achievable but demanding rigorous optimisation — precisely the role of the 36-month simulation programme.

