## 11. CONCLUSION AND FALSIFIABLE COMMITMENT

The Solar Synthetic Tree v4.0 is a layered engineering hypothesis, now anchored in six 2025–2026 scientific and regulatory developments that together move the concept from speculative to computationally tractable. The 33.6 % flexible tandem canopy is experimentally certified. The conductive Electro-MOF contactor with 96 % Faradaic efficiency is peer-reviewed. The solid-electrolyte DAE reactor operating at 0.6 V is demonstrated. The EU CRCF DACCS methodology is in force. The PINN for electrochemical systems achieves < 1.2 % error relative to high-fidelity models. The vLLM inference framework delivers 7B-parameter LLM inference at ≈ 8 W on a production edge server.

This PhD will reduce these developments to a set of coupled differential equations, electrochemical models, material databases, federated learning code, and a fine-tuned domain language model — tested rigorously against the best available operational data, and constrained to succeed or fail by three simultaneous falsifiable criteria:

**1. Net-carbon-negative:** A single SST unit captures more CO₂ over its 20-year simulated life than was emitted during its manufacture, within ≤ 4 years of desert operation, verified by independent third-party LCA conforming to EU CRCF QU.A.L.ITY criteria.

**2. LLM-orchestrated superiority:** A fleet of 100 simulated SST nodes governed by the LLM-augmented hierarchy captures ≥ 10 % more CO₂ per unit energy than a rule-based controller under identical climate forcing.

**3. Economic viability:** The levelised cost of carbon removal is ≤ €180 t⁻¹ under mid-range climate assumptions, competitive with 2026 commercial electrochemical DAC, while delivering measurable and independently verified co-benefits in cooling, water, and biodiversity.

Only when all three are demonstrated *in silico* will the project advance to physical prototyping and experimental collaboration.

The future city may not only contain trees. It may itself begin to think like a forest — a forest built on equations that do not forgive approximation, governed by a mind that speaks every human language, and rooted in chemistry that turns air into stone.

